/**
\mainpage
\htmlinclude manifest.html

\b underwater_vehicle_sim models and simulated autonomous underwater vehicles.
Each vehicle is modelled using a collection of modules. Two types of modules exist,
general modules and propulsion modules. General modules define behaviors and capabilities
of the vehicles. A vehicle can have any number of general modules. Propulsion modules define
the operation of the propulsion system of the vehicle. Only one propulsion module is used per
vehicle. Each module contains an update function which is called at a specified rate.

The package also contains a clock_server node which publishes the /clock message at a specified rate.
This rate can be modified programmatically using a topic.


